  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2021-12-30T12:38:20.578Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Played audio from UDON will be delayed.\nI have tested the audio system for making a rhythm game.\nWhen I test that playing audio on pulling triggers in VR, the sound will reach me delayed (maybe around 0.2 seconds later).\nExcept if strict audio timing is required, the delay is no problem but in my situation requires playing a sound as soon as possible.\nI need the sound to arrive within 0.05 seconds ideally.\n(For example, a traditional piano is 0.04 seconds.)\nOf course, I understand that some reasons cause this delay.\nBut it might improve a bit by specifying the DSP Buffer Size in the Unity project settings.\nThe Oculus Audio SDK document recommends the DSP Buffer Size set to \"Best latency\" for PC and \"Good latency\" for Quest.\nIMHO, recommend setting to \"Good latency\" to avoid audio jitters on low spec PC.\nhttps://developer.oculus.com/documentation/unity/audio-osp-unity-req-setup/#enable-the-oculus-spatializer\nA test world is available at https://vrchat.com/home/world/wrld_061600a7-411e-4340-920c-1df8f7597f76\nTo reproduce the problem:\n1. Press the Ding button to play sounds repeatedly.\n2. Pull the trigger of a controller at that ding sound.\n3. You'll hear the delayed click sound from the ding sound.\nAnd I created its unitypackage but I don't know where to upload it.\nCould you tell me where to upload it?",
